/// reply, and this function publishes one ITSELF before returning `true` — so
/// an Alloy handler that also returns a reply answers the same request twice.
/// The symptom is subtle: the gate's refusal is what the caller sees, and the
/// second reply is silently discarded, so the app looks correct while every
/// gated request costs two publishes. Alloy applications call [`gate`] and
/// return the reply it hands back.
///
/// [`gate`] hands back a reply for the caller to publish, which suits a
/// framework that already owns that step. A bare `FerriteApp` loop varies too
